<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Östergötland</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as East Gothland</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Östergötland is a historical province in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-vattern">Lake Vättern</a>, with Linköping and Norrköping as its main towns. One of the heartlands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geats">Geats</a>, it holds the Rök runestone and Vadstena Abbey, founded by Saint Bridget. In the 12th and 13th centuries it was a power base of rival royal families in the making of the Swedish kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ostergotland.jpg" alt="Östergötland" width="320" height="729" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lapplänning (highlighting by Lokal_Profil) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sverigekarta-Landskap_%C3%96sterg%C3%B6tland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
